From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0008] rtos: re-arm bulk-IN urb on unknown completion status

The completion default branch (and nothing else in the error switch)
neither recycled nor re-armed the recvbuf - on this stack the codes
reaching it are -ETIMEDOUT / -ENOMEM / -EIO (lkpi_usb_errno over the
cherryusb xHCI errorcodes), all transient.  Each occurrence permanently
removed one bulk-IN urb from the RX pipeline; 8 urbs drained = the
"entire RX incl. completions frozen" stall form (issues/
2026-10-03-rtl8821cu-rx-queue-stall.md form 2).  Re-arm like the
-EPROTO family; the pre-existing continual_io_error check above the
switch bounds the loop via surprise-removed.  [W11-C2]
---
--- a/os_dep/linux/usb_ops_linux.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/usb_ops_linux.c
@@ -947,10 +947,15 @@
 			rtw_rxdbg_comp(RTW_RXDBG_C_OTHER, precvbuf->pskb, precvbuf);	/* [W4-fix probe] */
 			break;
 		default:
-			/* [W6 probe]: the silent lifecycle hole (counted only;
-			 * the W4 print here was withdrawn with the print
-			 * probes - read the counter via wlan8821 status) */
+			/* [W11-C2] close the silent lifecycle hole: on this
+			 * stack the codes landing here are -ETIMEDOUT /
+			 * -ENOMEM / -EIO (lkpi_usb_errno), all transient -
+			 * re-arm like the -EPROTO family instead of leaking
+			 * the recvbuf (the RX pipeline shrinks permanently
+			 * otherwise).  Bounded: the continual_io_error check
+			 * above trips surprise-removed if this repeats. */
 			rtw_rxdbg_comp(RTW_RXDBG_C_OTHER, precvbuf->pskb, precvbuf);
+			rtw_read_port(padapter, precvpriv->ff_hwaddr, 0, (unsigned char *)precvbuf);
 			break;
 		}
 	}
